  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting sustainability and international trade competence of Cameroonian national products by enhancing advanced technologies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Japan-funded project &quot;Promoting public health by improving the national supply chain capacity for medical products for increased resilience against COVID-19&quot;(SAP 210174) was successfuly implemented by UNIDO from April 2022 to August 2023. As part of the communication with the donor focal point, UNIDO indicated, in late 2022, our readiness as well as aspiration to develop a futrue project to continue the project-level committment to the national development agenda in the framework of Japan-UNIDO partnership.   Although UNIDO team conitunuously followed up the status of the discussion, there had been no advancement and updates from the donor side due to their limited financial availability allocated to Cameroon. The discussion about the future funding reopened in the end of 2023 by Japan as a potentially available fund had been identified. The donor focal point verbally/informally expressed that the primary targets of the fund are 1)business/trade partnership with the donor in the context of private sector development; 2)well-alingned objectives with other ongoing committment by Japan; 3) to catalyze sustainable technologies in industrial contexts. The budget size will be dependant on the available budget in the donor#s planning and it is expected to be influenced by other projects as well. Based on the commu</narrative>
  </description>
